{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1594 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9bb3d809ae7b572394d6eb86ef22805429d4e9c58e47f9de02ae85440f76ac0e" :edb/db-before-t 1593 :edb/db-after-t 1594 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534906 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:39:37.852Z" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119426 1100 "Calculate\n$\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 10 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix}$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119426 1100 "Calculate \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/26dbd9a28532c3c262ca8015444364febabb8e269e5c6310a8fc59268f6e215c.png)" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119426 1145 "The determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix} &= (-2) \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot (-2) = 4\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119426 1145 "The determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 10 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =(-2)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-2)=4\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119427 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 19 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119427 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/28a22a5f860f02e42abc699e9807de885cc01b572c23ac0d4f909fe281042e08.png)" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119427 1145 "Notice that the $1$st column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 5 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 19 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (-1)^{1 + 1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{vmatrix} &= 1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (-3) =-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 2 \\cdot (-6) = -12\n$$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119427 1145 "Notice that the $1$st column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 19 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 2 \\cdot (-6) = -12.\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119428 1100 "Given that $\\det(A)=4$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\textrm{det}(A^T)=16$\n2. $3\\textrm{det}(A^T)=12$\n3. $\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)=17$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119428 1100 "Given that $\\det(A)=4,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)=16$\n\n- $3\\textrm{det}(A^T)=12$\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)=17$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119428 1145 "From the properties of determinants, we know that\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=\\textrm{det}(A)=4\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(I)=1\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Rather,\n$\\textrm{det}(A^T)=4 \\neq 16$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n$3\\textrm{det}(A^T)= 3 \\cdot 4 = 12$.\n- Statement III is false. We have\n$\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)= 4 + 1 = 5 \\neq 17$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139534906 false] [17592186119428 1145 "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=\\textrm{det}(A)=4\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Rather, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=4 \\neq 16.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\textrm{det}(A^T)= 3 \\cdot 4 = 12.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)= 4 + 1 = 5 \\neq 17.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139534906 true] [17592186119429 1100 "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/47850d3c530a29de8cb5df4bb3e035b9e29fb1ba65ff0eca2d39e6d8e0a2b06b.png)" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119429 1100 "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119429 1145 "First, let's construct the matrix $M$, whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, $\\mathbf{c}$, and $\\mathbf{d}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M{:}$\n\n$$\nV = \\mid \\det(M) \\mid\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(M) &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-1)^{2 + 1}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3 \\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(M) &= -3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-1)^{2 + 2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-3(15 + 4) \\\\\n&=-57\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV = \\begin{vmatrix}\\det(M) & = & -57\\end{vmatrix} = 57\n$$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186119429 1145 "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043085/assets/0563d565dff1928d21da21ad832fad37f94fb385ddb8a805423ae2577ae9434c.png)\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M{:}$\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) |\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3 \\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(15+4) \\\\  & =-57.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) | = |-57| = 57.\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186119850 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318700 13194139534906 true] [17592186119850 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318784 13194139534906 true] [17592186119850 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318791 13194139534906 true] [17592186119850 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318798 13194139534906 true] [17592186119850 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318805 13194139534906 true] [17592186119851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318707 13194139534906 true] [17592186119851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318714 13194139534906 true] [17592186119851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318777 13194139534906 true] [17592186119851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318812 13194139534906 true] [17592186119851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318819 13194139534906 true] [17592186119852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318721 13194139534906 true] [17592186119852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318728 13194139534906 true] [17592186119852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318770 13194139534906 true] [17592186119852 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318826 13194139534906 true] [17592186119853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318735 13194139534906 true] [17592186119853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318742 13194139534906 true] [17592186119853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318749 13194139534906 true] [17592186119853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318756 13194139534906 true] [17592186119853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318763 13194139534906 true] [17592186120354 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534906 true] [17592186120354 1100 "Given that $det(A^{T}) = 5$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $4det(A) = 20$\n2. $2det(A^{T}) = 25$\n3. $det(A) - 3det(I) = 8$" 13194139534906 false] [17592186120354 1100 "Given that $det({A}^{T})=5$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4\\text{det}(A)=20$\n- $2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=25$\n- $\\text{det}(A)-3\\text{det}(I)=8$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186120354 1145 "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)=\\text{det}({A}^{T})=5\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n4\\text{det}(A)=4\\cdot 5=20.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=2\\cdot 5=10\\ne 25.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-3\\text{det}(I)=5-3\\cdot 1=2\\ne 8.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318701 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1089 "q-130238" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1100 "Consider the matrices $A$ and $B$ given below. Find $det(A)-det({B}^{T}).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1.5 & 7.4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1113 #uuid "995633e5-96ca-5496-ba79-bcf6ece6ec56" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318700 1145 "The determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(2)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 1=-4 \\\\ det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1.5 & 7.4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|=3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, $det({B}^{T})=det(B)=-6.$ \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(A)-det({B}^{T})=-4-(-6)=2.\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318702 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318703 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318704 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318705 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318706 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1041 "selection" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318703 13194139534906 true] [17592186318701 1110 #uuid "7bde7827-1970-51f4-b683-0eaff179440e" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318702 1034 "3" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318702 1111 #uuid "333beb15-8dd4-58b0-b5cb-6ac68da294e0" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318703 1034 "2" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318703 1111 #uuid "3d2385c4-13a2-5efa-9928-4b9b11badb71" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318704 1034 "1" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318704 1111 #uuid "e169793d-5814-5cb1-9258-ca8598002033" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318705 1034 "4" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318705 1111 #uuid "1b50ce1b-bb77-5fac-bfeb-f925f83c29ec" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318706 1034 "5" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318706 1111 #uuid "2aa28d9f-79cd-5830-9cab-54f693422cff" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318708 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1089 "q-130292" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1113 #uuid "bc7bb8a5-4e30-5286-a345-3410950b7e92" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318707 1145 "Notice that the $3$rd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)=-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-60.\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318709 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318710 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318711 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318712 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318713 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1041 "selection" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318713 13194139534906 true] [17592186318708 1110 #uuid "0fc96394-b747-54f9-8d1e-5b34af8e98dc" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318709 1034 "15" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318709 1111 #uuid "47eb2c69-1413-513a-b390-8f44c6607b84" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318710 1034 "-30" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318710 1111 #uuid "ed08d8bb-424c-56c8-9f8a-3354e28cc0cf" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318711 1034 "-45" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318711 1111 #uuid "7788f4d9-25a8-5ad7-95b0-1a6d93e2537d" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318712 1034 "30" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318712 1111 #uuid "fd7c8c9b-a40b-5ced-8c20-7de46d6d90c1" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318713 1034 "-60" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534906 true] [17592186318713 1111 #uuid "9e2b317f-a93c-5e7e-aa47-e6c3d41bd083" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318715 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1089 "q-130320" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,\\,-2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1113 #uuid "6cc689f5-55a8-5819-befb-256bf286c074" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318714 1145 "Notice that the $3$rd row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (3\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-12\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-12(10-6) \\\\  & =(-12)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534906 true] [17592186318715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318716 13194139534906 true] [1759218631871